        <detaileddescription>
<para>Argument name. The name is used for documentation and error messages. It need not look like a variable. For instance, it could be &quot;on|off|auto&quot; to indicate that three values are possible, or &quot;\@v{int}|wide&quot; to indicate that the value can be any integer or the string &quot;wide&quot;. The string may contain markup, which is removed when used in error messages. As a convenience, if the string begins with a lower-case letter and contains only lower-case letters, hyphens, and underscores then it will be treated as a variable. That is, the string &quot;foo&quot; is shorthand for &quot;\@v{foo}&quot;. </para>        </detaileddescription>
